+### [Renderer configuration](3272-renderer-configuration.md)
+The Renderer configuration is a top-level controller that manages global rendering parameters such as ray depth, sampling rates, and background color. It serves as the static interface for adjusting image-order rendering behavior, including exposure, gamma correction, and post-processing flags like FXAA, diffuse shading, shadows, and Screen Space Ambient Occlusion (SSAO). It differs from sibling methods by centralizing these global state variables rather than implementing the ray traversal or shading logic itself.
 
